  {
    "id" : "scss_at-if-no-null",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Explicit Equality Comparison to Null in Sass",
    "description" : "Disallow explicit equality comparisons to null in Sass @if statements as null is falsey by default.",
    "explanation" : "# at-if-no-null\n\nCheck for equality to null is unnecessarily explicit since `null` is falsey in Sass.\n\n```scss\na {\n    @if $x == null {}\n/**         ↑     ↑\n * == or != null is unncessary */\n}\n```\n\n## Options\n\ntrue\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n```scss\na {\n    @if $x == null {}\n}\n```\n\n```scss\na {\n    @if $x != null {}\n}\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```scss\na {\n    @if $x {}\n}\n```\n\n```scss\na {\n    @if not $x {}\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-if-no-null",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "at-if-no-null"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_at-import-no-partial-leading-underscore",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Leading Underscore in Partial Names in @import",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of a leading underscore in partial file names within SCSS @import statements.",
    "explanation" : "# at-import-no-partial-leading-underscore\n\nDisallow leading underscore in partial names in `@import`.\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/to/_file\"\n/**              ↑\n *   Disallow this */\n```\n\nThe rule ignores [cases](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/import) when Sass considers an `@import` command just a plain CSS import:\n\n* If the file’s extension is `.css`.\n* If the filename begins with `http://` (or any other protocol).\n* If the filename is a `url()`.\n* If the `@import` has any media queries.\n\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"_foo\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/_fff\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path\\\\_fff\"; /* Windows delimiters */\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"df/fff\", '_1.scss';\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"_path/fff\"; /* underscore in a directory name, not in a partial name */\n```\n\n```scss\n@import url(\"path/_file.css\"); /* has url(), so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"_file.css\"; /* Has \".css\" extension, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n/* Both are URIs, so don't count as partial @imports */\n@import \"http://_file.scss\";\n@import \"//_file.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"_file.scss\" screen; /* Has a media query, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-import-no-partial-leading-underscore",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "at-import-no-partial-leading-underscore"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_at-import-partial-extension",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Require or Disallow Extension in @import Commands",
    "description" : "Enforces whether file extensions should be included or omitted in SCSS @import statements.",
    "explanation" : "# at-import-partial-extension\n\nRequire or disallow extension in `@import` commands.\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.scss\";\n/**           ↑\n * This extension */\n```\n\nThe [`fix` option](https://stylelint.io/user-guide/usage/options#fix) can automatically fix all of the problems reported by this rule only when `\"never\"` is given.\n\nThe rule ignores [cases](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/import) when Sass considers an `@import` command just a plain CSS import:\n\n- If the file’s extension is `.css`.\n- If the filename begins with `http://` (or any other protocol).\n- If the filename is a `url()`.\n- If the `@import` has any media queries.\n\n## Options\n\n`string`: `\"always\"|\"never\"`\n\n### `\"always\"`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"foo\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/fff\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path\\\\fff\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"df/fff\", \"1.SCSS\";\n```\n\nThe following patterns are _not_ considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"fff.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/fff.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import url(\"path/_file.css\"); /* has url(), so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.css\"; /* Has \".css\" extension, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n/* Both are URIs, so don't count as partial @imports */\n@import \"http://_file.scss\";\n@import \"//_file.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.scss\" screen; /* Has a media query, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n### `\"never\"`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"foo.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/fff.less\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path\\\\fff.ruthless\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"df/fff\", \"1.SCSS\";\n```\n\nThe following patterns are _not_ considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"foo\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/fff\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import url(\"path/_file.css\"); /* has url(), so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.css\"; /* Has \".css\" extension, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n/* Both are URIs, so don't count as partial @imports */\n@import \"http://_file.scss\";\n@import \"//_file.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.scss\" screen; /* Has a media query, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-import-partial-extension",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "at-import-partial-extension"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_at-import-partial-extension-allowed-list",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Allowed File Extensions for Partial Names in @import Commands",
    "description" : "This rule enforces a specified list of allowed file extensions for partial names used in `@import` commands in SCSS files.",
    "explanation" : "# at-import-partial-extension-allowed-list\n\nSpecify a list of allowed file extensions for partial names in `@import` commands.\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.scss\"\n/**           ↑\n * Allowed list of these */\n```\n\nThe rule ignores [cases](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/import) when Sass considers an `@import` command just a plain CSS import:\n\n* If the file’s extension is `.css`.\n* If the filename begins with `http://` (or any other protocol).\n* If the filename is a `url()`.\n* If the `@import` has any media queries.\n\n## Options\n\n`array`: `[\"array\", \"of\", \"extensions\"]`\n\nEach value is either a string or a regexp.\n\nGiven:\n\n```js\n[\"scss\", /less/]\n```\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.sass\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file1\", \"file.stylus\";\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/fff\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"foo.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path/fff.less\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"path\\\\fff.ruthless\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"df/fff\", '1.SCSS';\n```\n\n```scss\n@import url(\"path/_file.css\"); /* has url(), so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.css\"; /* Has \".css\" extension, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```\n\n```scss\n/* Both are URIs, so don't count as partial @imports */\n@import \"http://_file.scss\";\n@import \"//_file.scss\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@import \"file.scss\" screen; /* Has a media query, so doesn't count as a partial @import */\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-import-partial-extension-allowed-list",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "at-import-partial-extension-allowed-list"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
