  {
    "id" : "scss_at-rule-conditional-no-parentheses",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Parentheses in SCSS Conditional At-Rules",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of parentheses in SCSS conditional at-rules such as @if, @elsif, and @while.",
    "explanation" : "# at-rule-conditional-no-parentheses\n\nDisallow parentheses in conditional @ rules (if, elsif, while)\n\n```css\n    @if (true) {}\n/**     ↑    ↑\n * Get rid of parentheses like this. */\n```\n\nThe [`fix` option](https://stylelint.io/user-guide/usage/options#fix) can automatically fix all of the problems reported by this rule.\n\n## Options\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@if(true)\n```\n\n```scss\n@else if(true)\n```\n\n```scss\n@while(true)\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@if true\n```\n\n```scss\n@else if true\n```\n\n```scss\n@while true\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-rule-conditional-no-parentheses",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "at-rule-conditional-no-parentheses"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_at-rule-no-unknown",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Unknown At-Rules in SCSS",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of unknown or unsupported at-rules in SCSS stylesheets, preventing warnings for SCSS-specific directives like @if and @extend.",
    "explanation" : "# at-rule-no-unknown\n\nDisallow unknown at-rules. Should be used **instead of** Stylelint's [at-rule-no-unknown](https://stylelint.io/user-guide/rules/at-rule-no-unknown).\n\n```css\n    @unknown (max-width: 960px) {}\n/** ↑\n * At-rules like this */\n```\n\nThis rule is basically a wrapper around the mentioned core rule, but with added SCSS-specific `@`-directives. So if you use the core rule, `@if`, `@extend` and other Sass-y things will get warnings. You must disable Stylelint's core rule to make this rule work:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"at-rule-no-unknown\": null,\n    \"scss/at-rule-no-unknown\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Options\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```css\n@unknown {}\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```css\n@function foo () {}\n```\n\n```css\n@while ($i == 1) {}\n```\n\n```css\n@media (max-width: 960px) {}\n```\n\n```css\n@if ($i) {} @else {}\n```\n\n## Optional secondary options\n\n### `ignoreAtRules: [\"/regex/\", \"string\"]`\n\nGiven:\n\n```js\n[\"/^my-/i\", \"custom\"]\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```css\n@my-at-rule \"x.css\";\n```\n\n```css\n@my-other-at-rule {}\n```\n\n```css\n@MY-OTHER-AT-RULE {}\n```\n\n```css\n@custom {}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-rule-no-unknown",
        "default" : "true",
        "description" : "at-rule-no-unknown"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_at-use-no-redundant-alias",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Redundant Namespace Aliases in SCSS @use",
    "description" : "This rule disallows redundant namespace aliases in SCSS @use statements where the alias is the same as the module's default namespace name.",
    "explanation" : "# at-use-no-redundant-alias\n\nDisallow redundant namespace aliases.\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\" as foo;\n/**           ↑\n * Disallow this */\n```\n\nBy default, the [module's namespace](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/use/#loading-members)\nis the last component of the module’s URL.\n\n## Options\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\" as foo;\n```\n\n```scss\n@use \"sass:math\" as math;\n```\n\n```scss\n@use \"src/corners\" as corners;\n```\n\nThe following patterns are _not_ considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\" as bar;\n```\n\n```scss\n@use \"sass:math\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@use \"src/corners\" as c;\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "at-use-no-redundant-alias",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "at-use-no-redundant-alias"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_at-use-no-unnamespaced",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow usage of @use without a namespace",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the usage of the SCSS `@use` directive with a wildcard namespace (`as *`), enforcing explicit namespacing.",
    "explanation" : "# at-use-no-unnamespaced\n\nDisallow usage of `@use` without a namespace.\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\" as *;\n/**           ↑\n * Disallow this */\n```\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\" as *;\n```\n\nThe following patterns are _not_ considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\";\n```\n\n```scss\n@use \"foo\" as bar;\n```",
