  {
    "id" : "scss_block-no-redundant-nesting",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Redundant Nesting in SCSS Blocks",
    "description" : "This rule disallows nesting a single SCSS block inside a parent block when the nested block could be merged directly with the parent block's selector.",
    "explanation" : "# block-no-redundant-nesting\n\nDisallow nesting a single block if it could be merged with its parent block.\n\n```scss\n.foo {\n  .bar {}\n}\n```\n\n[Sass official docs on nested properties](https://sass-lang.com/documentation/style-rules/declarations#nesting).\n\n## Options\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n.foo {\n  .bar {}\n}\n```\n\n```scss\n.foo {\n  &-bar {\n    &-baz {\n      color: red;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n.foo .bar {}\n```\n\n```scss\n.foo-bar-baz {\n  color: red;\n}\n```\n\n```scss\n// multiple child blocks\n.foo {\n  .bar {}\n  &-baz {}\n}\n```\n\n```scss\n// parent or child with selector list\n.foo {\n  .bar, .baz {}\n}\n\n.foo, .bar {\n  &-baz {}\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "block-no-redundant-nesting",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "block-no-redundant-nesting"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_comment-no-empty",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Empty Comments in SCSS",
    "description" : "This rule disallows empty comments in SCSS code, including both block and single-line comments.",
    "explanation" : "# comment-no-empty\n\nDisallow empty comments. Should be used **instead of** the Stylelint's [comment-no-empty](https://stylelint.io/user-guide/rules/comment-no-empty) because the core rule ignores SCSS-like comments.\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n    /* */\n    //\n```\n\nTo avoid duplicate issues, you must disable the core rule as follows:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"comment-no-empty\": null,\n    \"scss/comment-no-empty\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Options\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered violations:\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n/**/\n```\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n/* */\n```\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n/*\n\n */\n```\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n//\n```\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\nwidth: 10px; //\n```\n\nThe following patterns are _not_ considered violations:\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n/* comment */\n```\n\n<!-- prettier-ignore -->\n```scss\n/*\n * Multi-line Comment\n**/\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "comment-no-empty",
        "default" : "true",
        "description" : "comment-no-empty"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "scss_comment-no-loud",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Block Comments",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of block comments (`/* ... */`) and enforces the use of double-slash comments (`// ...`) in SCSS files.",
    "explanation" : "# comment-no-loud\n\nDisallow `/*`-comments.\n\n```scss\n/*  Comment */\n//  ↑     ↑\n// This line\n```\n\nThis rule only works on CSS comments (`/* */`) and ignores all double-slash (`//`) comments.\n\n## Options\n\n### `true`\n\nThe following patterns are considered violations:\n\n```scss\n/* comment */\n```\n\n```scss\n/*\n * comment\n*/\n```\n\nThe following patterns are *not* considered warnings:\n\n```scss\n// comment\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "comment-no-loud",
        "default" : "null",
        "description" : "comment-no-loud"
      }
