  {
    "id" : "selector-pseudo-class-focus",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce presence of :focus pseudo-class when using :hover",
    "description" : "Ensures that any CSS selector using the :hover pseudo-class also includes the :focus pseudo-class to improve accessibility and keyboard navigation.",
    "explanation" : "# selector-pseudo-class-focus\n\nChecks the presence of a pseudo-class for selectors with `:hover`.\n\n```css\na:hover,\na:focus {\n}\n```\n\nThis rule considers :focus pseudo-class selector defined in the CSS Specifications.\nThe `--fix` option on the command line can automatically fix all of the problems reported by this rule.\n\n## Options\n\n### true\n\nThe following pattern are considered violations:\n\n```css\na:hover {\n}\n```\n\nThe following patterns are _not_ considered violations:\n\n```css\na:hover,\na:focus {\n}\n```\n\n```css\na:focus {\n}\n```\n\n```css\na:hover {\n}\na:focus {\n}\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
